# ============================================================================
# FOSS Mavelli Hunt - environment
#
# REAL MODE (deployed event):
#   The app talks to Supabase ONLY through the Next.js API routes, which use
#   the service-role key on the server. The client never holds any Supabase
#   key. The anon key is deliberately NOT used anymore (database access is
#   revoked for anon in schema.db M004).
#
# DEMO MODE (local testing, no backend):
#   Leave NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL unset. The app runs on localStorage in a
#   single browser - no database needed.
# ============================================================================

# --- mode switch (client build-time) --------------------------------------
# Used ONLY to tell the client which store to use. Not secret (it is the
# public project URL), but do not prefix secrets with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=

# --- server-only secrets (NEVER prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_) -----------------
# Find these in Supabase: Project Settings -> API.
# The service role key bypasses RLS - it must never leave the server.
# On Vercel add these in Project Settings -> Environment Variables, and
# NEVER commit them.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- real mode setup (one-time) -------------------------------------------
# 1. Create a Supabase project (free tier).
# 2. SQL Editor: run schema.db (repo root) - idempotent, safe to re-run.
# 3. SQL Editor: run supabase/seed.sql - loads placeholder content.
# 4. Copy the values above into .env.local (or Vercel env vars).
# 5. Replace placeholder content in supabase/seed.sql before the event
#    (words, photos, Mapillary links, BitChat code, admin code, volunteer
#    numbers).
